-- 134: GATE N2-A -- misprediction visibility MEASURED. Follows 117/119/120/122/124/130/132.
-- Source doc: mvc-live-skins-quarters/docs/SUPERGUN-NETCODE.md s13. Harness d3dcap/net/sg_n2.py (netcode lane, new).
-- Method step 4. Lane numbering: SUPERGUN NETCODE takes EVEN numbers from 120 up.
-- Apply with tools/re_kb/apply_seed.py after the README export backup (re_kb_data/_exports/*_pre134.surql).
-- Idempotent and order-independent. No apostrophes in literals. Do NOT re-run 07_dedup_edges.surql afterwards.
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:supergun_gate_n2a_20260904 SET kind='measurement', strength='reproduction', ref='mvc-live-skins-quarters/d3dcap/net/sg_n2.py run against d3dcap/ttd/runs/receipt-20260903-stage9-anchor/pre with %TEMP%/rrcap_runner/gate2_300/inputs.txt; output %TEMP%/sg_n2a/n2a.json (game-derived, never committed)', note='One truth run of 300 ticks with real inputs dumping every tick, then 25 mispredicted runs (start frames 20 to 260 step 10, depth 30) in which ticks at or after the start hold the seat-0 word from the previous frame. State at start+j is exactly what a player would see after j frames of misprediction, so one run yields every depth. Comparison is on the fighter pool px, py and hp decoded at blk+0x3DB8+i*0x738 offsets 0x50, 0x54 and 0x578, guarded by cid at 0x6C0.';

UPSERT finding:supergun_n2_naive_would_be_confounded SET status='confirmed', text='THE OBVIOUS GATE N2 WOULD HAVE BEEN A CONFOUNDED GATE, AND IT WOULD HAVE PASSED LOUDLY. Every input tape in this project has the REMOTE seat identically zero: all five files at %TEMP%/rrcap_runner/*/inputs.txt have a seat1 distinct-value set of exactly {0}, because the stage-9 receipt is one-sided. Repeat-last prediction of an all-zero stream is exactly right on every frame BY CONSTRUCTION, so running N2 as specified on the only available data would have reported ZERO visible divergence at every depth and been written up as prediction is free, push the speculation cap as deep as you like. That is the project signature failure mode -- a gate that passes because it is measuring nothing -- and the input data, not the harness, is what makes it so. Checked before the harness was built rather than after the result looked good.';

UPSERT finding:supergun_gate_n2a_result SET status='confirmed', text='GATE N2-A RESULT (mispredicting seat 0, whose inputs are real: non-idle on 132 of 300 frames). Calibration taken from the truth run itself so the numbers mean something: stage extent 2,174 world units in px (range -1386.7 to 787.5) and median per-frame movement 7.95 units when a fighter is moving, so divergence is also expressed as FRAMES OF NORMAL MOVEMENT. Worst |dpx| p90 / max, and max as frames-of-movement, at 25 samples per depth: depth 1 = 0.00 / 5.83 / 0.7; depth 2 = 0.00 / 8.75 / 1.1; depth 4 = 0.00 / 14.58 / 1.8; depth 8 = 5.83 / 26.25 / 3.3; depth 12 = 40.03 / 66.67 / 8.4; depth 16 = 75.62 / 133.33 / 16.8; depth 24 = 144.37 / 235.83 / 29.6; depth 30 = 197.50 / 272.50 / 34.3 (12.5 percent of the stage). dhp is ZERO at every depth below 24 and 7 at depths 24 to 30. blk differs on 16 percent of samples at depth 1 rising to 64 percent at depth 30. THREE CONCLUSIONS. (1) THE DISTRIBUTION IS BIMODAL AND THE MEDIAN IS ZERO AT EVERY DEPTH: |dpx| p50 is 0.000 from depth 1 to depth 30, so most of the time repeat-last is exactly right and the misprediction costs nothing; the entire cost lives in the tail. (2) BIT-ACCURACY IS THE WRONG METRIC, NOW MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSERTED: at depth 8 repeat-last is bit-correct on only 68 percent of frames yet the median visible divergence is zero and p90 is 5.8 units, a quarter of one frame of movement, so most wrong predictions change nothing a player can see and anyone tuning a predictor on input-bit accuracy optimises the wrong quantity. (3) d = 0 IS SUPPORTED AT NORMAL RTT: in steady state the rollback depth is owd rather than the cap, and at owd of 4 frames or less (133 ms RTT or less) the worst displacement over 25 start points is 14.6 units = 1.8 frames of movement = 0.7 percent of the stage, with a median of zero and no HP divergence at all.';

UPSERT finding:supergun_n2a_is_a_lower_bound SET status='confirmed', text='THE CAVEAT THAT MATTERS MOST ABOUT N2-A, AND IT CUTS AGAINST THE RESULT. Because seat 1 is idle there is NO OPPONENT TO REACT TO, so every divergence measured is pure my-character-ended-up-somewhere-else with NO compounding through hit, block or hitstun interactions -- and the data shows exactly that signature, since dhp is ZERO at every depth below 24. In real two-sided play an 8-frame misprediction can flip a hit into a block or a whiff into a counter-hit, and the resulting state difference is not a few units of position but a combo that happened versus one that did not, worth hundreds of HP and a different animation on both characters. N2-A THEREFORE ALMOST CERTAINLY UNDERSTATES DIVERGENCE FOR REAL TWO-SIDED PLAY AND ITS NUMBERS ARE A FLOOR, NOT AN EXPECTATION. Nobody may quote 3.3 frames of movement at depth 8 as the expected artefact in a real match. Other limits, stated so the table is not over-read: one stage (9), one input stream, 25 start points, depth 30 maximum, repeat-last only with no alternative predictor tested, and no super or hyper in the input stream (the same gap as U-S2).';

UPSERT finding:supergun_speculation_cap_is_a_recovery_ceiling SET status='confirmed', text='DESIGN CONSEQUENCE OF N2-A, AND IT CHANGES HOW THE SPECULATION CAP SHOULD BE READ. The cost table showed depth 30 at 1.3 ms p50, trivially affordable, which invites treating 30 as a normal operating point. N2-A says a depth-30 misprediction can put a fighter 272 units out of place: 12.5 percent of the stage, 34 frames of normal movement, an unmistakable teleport. THE SPECULATION CAP IS A LOSS-BURST RECOVERY CEILING, NOT A TARGET. The depth actually used in steady state is owd. Cheap CPU buys the ABILITY to recover from a 500 ms delivery gap without stalling; it does not make a 500 ms misprediction look acceptable. The alternative at that depth is a hard stall, so deep recovery remains the right choice -- but it is choosing the less-bad of two visible artefacts, not avoiding one. Corollary: CPU cost was never the binding constraint on speculation depth, exactly as finding:supergun_frame_delay_policy predicted before any of this was measured; misprediction visibility is, and it is now measured for one seat.';

UPSERT finding:supergun_gate_n2b_needed SET status='open', text='U-N12, GATE N2-B, and it is the top-priority open item of the netcode lane. Re-run d3dcap/net/sg_n2.py on a tape with TWO NON-IDLE SEATS, so that misprediction compounds through hit, block and hitstun interactions rather than only through position. BLOCKED ON DATA, NOT MACHINERY: the harness is written, works, and produced N2-A; no tape in the project has a non-idle remote seat. The right source is a recorded two-player tape from the CONFIRMED GGPO input ring (see rr-ggpo-input-ring: session *0x142E10B98, Sync+0x9F0, queues+0x190, stride 0xE44, read bounded by the confirmed watermark and never by _framecount), or failing that a synthesised opposing stream. UNTIL N2-B RUNS, THE MISPREDICTION QUESTION IS NOT CLOSED and the N2-A numbers must be quoted as a floor.';

UPSERT finding:supergun_gate_n2_predictor_comparison_open SET status='open', text='U-N13, predictor comparison. N2-A establishes the CONTROL -- repeat-last, measured on real inputs with a calibrated visible-delta metric -- but no alternative predictor has been run against it. The falsification stated in the design is unchanged and now has a baseline to beat: a candidate predictor that does not stochastically dominate repeat-last on visible state delta at EVERY depth does not help and is dropped. Candidates in order of what must be beaten: repeat-last (the control, now measured), decay-to-neutral after k frames, and a behaviour-cloned predictor conditioned on recent inputs and game state (the mvc2-ai pipeline exists but targets the DC/NAOMI build, so reusing it is a port and not a drop-in). Note from N2-A that the metric matters more than the candidate: tuning any of these on input-bit accuracy would optimise the wrong quantity, since at depth 8 repeat-last is only 68 percent bit-correct while its median visible divergence is zero.';

-- edges
RELATE finding:supergun_n2_naive_would_be_confounded->cites->source:supergun_gate_n2a_20260904 SET id=cites:n2a_confound_src;
RELATE finding:supergun_gate_n2a_result->cites->source:supergun_gate_n2a_20260904 SET id=cites:n2a_result_src;
RELATE finding:supergun_n2a_is_a_lower_bound->cites->source:supergun_gate_n2a_20260904 SET id=cites:n2a_lowerbound_src;
RELATE finding:supergun_speculation_cap_is_a_recovery_ceiling->cites->source:supergun_gate_n2a_20260904 SET id=cites:n2a_ceiling_src;
RELATE finding:supergun_gate_n2b_needed->cites->source:supergun_gate_n2a_20260904 SET id=cites:n2b_src;
RELATE finding:supergun_gate_n2_predictor_comparison_open->cites->source:supergun_gate_n2a_20260904 SET id=cites:n2_predictor_src;
RELATE finding:supergun_speculation_cap_is_a_recovery_ceiling->cites->finding:supergun_gate_n2a_result SET id=cites:ceiling_from_result;
RELATE finding:supergun_n2a_is_a_lower_bound->cites->finding:supergun_gate_n2a_result SET id=cites:lowerbound_from_result;

UPDATE finding:supergun_speculation_cap_specified SET note='READ WITH finding:supergun_speculation_cap_is_a_recovery_ceiling. The cost basis of this cap is CONFIRMED for simulation cost, but N2-A measured what the cost table cannot see: a depth-30 misprediction displaces a fighter by up to 12.5 percent of the stage. The cap is a loss-burst RECOVERY CEILING and not an operating point; the depth used in steady state is owd. Also still conditioned on the render budget, U-N10.';
UPDATE finding:supergun_frame_delay_policy SET note='SUPPORTED BY MEASUREMENT 2026-09-04. The d = 0 default is now backed by Gate N2-A: at owd of 4 frames or fewer the worst visible displacement over 25 start points is 1.8 frames of normal movement with a median of zero and no HP divergence. ALSO CONFIRMED BY THE SAME RUN is the claim this policy rested on, that visible state delta and not input bit-accuracy is the right metric: repeat-last is 68 percent bit-correct at depth 8 while its median visible divergence is zero. ⚠ N2-A mispredicts ONE seat because no tape has a non-idle remote seat, so its numbers are a FLOOR; see finding:supergun_n2a_is_a_lower_bound and the blocking item finding:supergun_gate_n2b_needed.';
